The Manhattan distance between two points (x1, y1) and (x2, y2) is the sum of the horizontal and vertical gaps, so the function computes |x1 - x2| with abs and adds |y1 - y2|. Tuple elements are accessed by the fixed indices 0 and 1; comparing a float with an integer is allowed. For (0, 0) with (3, 4) the result is 7, or 1 + 3; for two equal points the result is 0.

